# Lines the language sweep in check-docs.sh may not flag.
#
# Format: <path>%%<substring>
# A hit is suppressed when its path matches an entry and the matched line
# contains that entry's substring.
#
# Every entry carries a comment saying why. An entry without a reason is a
# pattern that was weakened rather than a case that was understood.
#
# Do not widen an entry to cover a class of lines. If a whole file legitimately
# contains German, that file is either a verbatim quote of external output or a
# sign that the language-en module does not fit this project.

# The "Rolle" example is the language rule explaining itself: it names the
# translation layer it exists to prevent.
CLAUDE.md%%("Rolle" in the text

# Skill descriptions carry literal trigger phrases in the languages they are
# spoken in. Translating them would stop the skill from being found.
.claude/skills/verify/SKILL.md%%description:

# English "falls back" collides with German "falls". The sweep matches whole
# words, so it cannot tell the two apart; these two lines are English.
internal/summary/prompts.go%%falls back to the video prompts
internal/summary/prompts_test.go%%unknown source falls back to video

# Same collision, three more English lines. They arrived with 92f85df
# (2026-08-30, shared summaries) and have failed check-docs on every run since.
internal/server/podcast_handlers.go%%falls back to the
internal/storage/prompts.go%%falls back to another user's row
internal/storage/users.go%%falls back to another user's, which is
